<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Tenggarong</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Tenggarong is a town in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/east-kalimantan">East Kalimantan</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/indonesia">Indonesia</a>, on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mahakam-river">Mahakam River</a> upstream from Samarinda, and the seat of Kutai Kartanegara Regency. The sultans of Kutai Kartanegara moved their capital there in 1782, and their former palace, built in 1936, now houses the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mulavarman">Mulawarman</a> Museum. The town hosts the Erau festival, a traditional celebration of the Kutai court.</p></div>
